ative.\n- **R: f4-g4** or **R: f4-f5** checks lose the rook immediately to Kxg4/Kxf5 with no compensation, as the rook is undefended.\n\nReason: **P: h2-h4** is the most forcing move, directly threatening mate via h5 and Rh4 while capitalizing on Black's king exposure. It avoids premature piece sacrifices and creates immediate, tangible threats that Black cannot easily parry, maximizing White's winning chances.\n\nAnswer: P: h2-h4"}
